      "title": "Career and Student Employment Services",
      "description": "Career and Student Employment Services | Western Michigan University Skip to main content Top links Apply A–Z Find People goWMU Visit Keywords Main navigation Academics Admissions Financial Aid Student Life Athletics Research Give Main Menu Close Menu Keywords Top links Apply A–Z Find People goWMU Visit Home Explore Career Options Student Resources Resumes Cover Letters Interviews Job Fair Preparation Services for Students Job Postings Career Academy Resume Reviews Virtual Practice Interviews Career Coaching Headshots Employers Post an Opportunity Internships Engage on Campus International Students Bronco Engagement Faculty and Staff Campus Employment For Students For Supervisors Pay Rates Work Study Student Appreciation Events Event Preparation Request a Presentation Career Outcomes About Us Directory Our Student Staff Contact Us Main navigation Academics Admissions Financial Aid Student Life Athletics Research Give Career and Student Employment Services Career and Student Employment Services Career coaching Become job search ready by attending career workshops, work on your resume at Career Lab, or scheduling an appointment to talk to a professional career coach. Schedule your appointment This is your home base for exploring career options, job searching, interviewing, negotiating and finding internships. All these resources are available to WMU students, employers hiring Broncos, WMU alumni, student-employee supervisors, WMU faculty and staff, and students’ families. Pride points 94% of graduates are working or continuing their education —2024-25 Career Outcomes Report Explore the data 4,000+ internships by major Explore internships 30,000 jobs posted Log in to Handshake 140+ industries covered for practice interviews Prep for a big Interview Skip to content Group menu sidebar Home Explore Career Options Student Resources Resumes Cover Letters Interviews Job Fair Preparation Services for Students Job Postings Career Academy Resume Reviews Virtual Practice Interviews Career Coaching Headshots Employers Post an Opportunity Internships Engage on Campus International Students Bronco Engagement Faculty and Staff Campus Employment For Students For Supervisors Pay Rates Work Study Student Appreciation Events Event Preparation Request a Presentation Career Outcomes About Us Directory Our Student Staff Contact Us Career and Student Employment Services Western Michigan University Kalamazoo MI 49008-5225 USA (269) 387-2745 Students and alumni No matter where you might be in the job search process, you can find the career guidance and help you need right here. Career resources We provide career tools and resources for undergraduate students to help them explore career options, get internship experience and polish their résumés and interviewing skills. Job search services Get the help you need in the way you want—engaging workshops, drop-in résumé reviews, virtual practice interviews, 1:1 career coaching, and professional headshots—all free for all students. Student employment Student employment opportunities are available for Broncos looking for on-campus and part-time jobs in the community that fit into their class schedules. Handshake Find an internship, student job or full-time position Focus 2 Identify your values and skills to find the right fit Development Guide Find info, samples and worksheets to guide your career search Big Interview Practice your interview skills virtually Virtual Tour Join us for our next job fair This is your opportunity to meet employers in your field of study and find the right job for you. See our calendar of events Other members of the Western community Employers We connect employers with students, faculty, staff and administration at Western. Faculty and staff We provide the tools for WMU faculty and staff to encourage and guide students along their career paths. Families Western provides family members with the resources they need to help guide their students’ career development. We’re here to help Need to talk to someone about reaching your career goals? Our career specialists are here and ready to help all Western students and alumni make the most out of your career journey. Contact us Apply now Schedule your visit Request info Footer menu Audiences Alumni and Donors Businesses Veterans Locations Grand Rapids Kalamazoo Online Education Stryker School of Medicine Services Accessibility Campus Safety Information and Resources Human Resources Maps Parking Western Michigan University Kalamazoo MI 49008-5200 USA (269) 387-1000 Contact WMU WMU Notice of Non-Discrimination Land Acknowledgment Statement © 2026 All rights reserved. Social"
