    "https://wmich.edu/career/students": {
      "title": "Job Search Resources",
      "description": "Job Search Resources | Career and Student Employment Services | Western Michigan University Skip to main content Top links Apply A–Z Find People goWMU Visit Keywords Main navigation Academics Admissions Financial Aid Student Life Athletics Research Give Main Menu Close Menu Keywords Top links Apply A–Z Find People goWMU Visit Home Explore Career Options Student Resources Resumes Cover Letters Interviews Job Fair Preparation Services for Students Job Postings Career Academy Resume Reviews Virtual Practice Interviews Career Coaching Headshots Employers Post an Opportunity Internships Engage on Campus International Students Bronco Engagement Faculty and Staff Campus Employment For Students For Supervisors Pay Rates Work Study Student Appreciation Events Event Preparation Request a Presentation Career Outcomes About Us Directory Our Student Staff Contact Us Main navigation Academics Admissions Financial Aid Student Life Athletics Research Give Career and Student Employment Services Job Search Resources Career and Student Employment Services Skip to content Group menu sidebar Home Explore Career Options Student Resources Resumes Cover Letters Interviews Job Fair Preparation Services for Students Job Postings Career Academy Resume Reviews Virtual Practice Interviews Career Coaching Headshots Employers Post an Opportunity Internships Engage on Campus International Students Bronco Engagement Faculty and Staff Campus Employment For Students For Supervisors Pay Rates Work Study Student Appreciation Events Event Preparation Request a Presentation Career Outcomes About Us Directory Our Student Staff Contact Us Career and Student Employment Services Western Michigan University Kalamazoo MI 49008-5225 USA (269) 387-2745 Job Search Resources Job Search Basics Resumes The standard chronological resume format is suitable for anyone. One page is common although it varies by major and extent of experience. Interviews Find tips on best practices to prepare for upcoming interviews and an explanation of the STAR method for structure answers to behavioral interview questions. Finding Jobs WMU posts all jobs employers send to the university to Handshake. There are other platforms that can also be helpful for broader seaches. Find out about them here. Job Fair Preparation Tips and tricks for making the most of Job Fairs! Job offers and career management Find out what to do once you have gotten a job offer and after when you start your first job. Personal Commercial A personal commercial (also known as an elevator speech, personal introduction, 30-second commercial, etc.) is a quick, effective way to make an impressive introduction. Cover Letters View the full Career Development Guide Career Development Guide Resources for specific groups Veterans /career/veterans International Students /career/students/international Students with disabilities /career/studentswithdisabilities Students of color /career/studentsofcolor LGBTQ Students /career/lgbt Graduate Students /career/graduatestudents Develop knowledge, skills, and abilities Discover your strengths Social Media Essential skills AI and Job Searches Experience-Driven Learning Experience-driven learning is WMU's brand of Experiential Education. Footer menu Audiences Alumni and Donors Businesses Veterans Locations Grand Rapids Kalamazoo Online Education Stryker School of Medicine Services Accessibility Campus Safety Information and Resources Human Resources Maps Parking Western Michigan University Kalamazoo MI 49008-5200 USA (269) 387-1000 Contact WMU WMU Notice of Non-Discrimination Land Acknowledgment Statement © 2026 All rights reserved. Social"
