      "description": "Help with your career or job search | Career and Student Employment Services | Western Michigan University Skip to main content Top links Apply A–Z Find People goWMU Visit Keywords Main navigation Academics Admissions Financial Aid Student Life Athletics Research Give Main Menu Close Menu Keywords Top links Apply A–Z Find People goWMU Visit Home Explore Career Options Student Resources Resumes Cover Letters Interviews Job Fair Preparation Services for Students Job Postings Career Academy Resume Reviews Virtual Practice Interviews Career Coaching Headshots Employers Post an Opportunity Internships Engage on Campus International Students Bronco Engagement Faculty and Staff Campus Employment For Students For Supervisors Pay Rates Work Study Student Appreciation Events Event Preparation Request a Presentation Career Outcomes About Us Directory Our Student Staff Contact Us Main navigation Academics Admissions Financial Aid Student Life Athletics Research Give Career and Student Employment Services Job Search Resources Help with your career or job search Career and Student Employment Services Skip to content Group menu sidebar Home Explore Career Options Student Resources Resumes Cover Letters Interviews Job Fair Preparation Services for Students Job Postings Career Academy Resume Reviews Virtual Practice Interviews Career Coaching Headshots Employers Post an Opportunity Internships Engage on Campus International Students Bronco Engagement Faculty and Staff Campus Employment For Students For Supervisors Pay Rates Work Study Student Appreciation Events Event Preparation Request a Presentation Career Outcomes About Us Directory Our Student Staff Contact Us Career and Student Employment Services Western Michigan University Kalamazoo MI 49008-5225 USA (269) 387-2745 Help with your career or job search Start Here Career Academy Career Academy is a series of four workshops where we empower students to stand out in a candidate pool. Complete the series and receive a professional padfolio . Join today and take the first step towards a successful career! Sign up for Career Academy either by attending any of the workshops listed below, or using the link and selecting \"Join\" through ExperienceWMU. Sign up for Career Academy Career Academy workshops are not offered during the summer and will begin in September 2026. Need help crafting a winning resume? Join this hands-on workshop to learn the basics of resume writing, including the standard chronological format and how to best highlight your accomplishments.   \n\nBring your laptop and your current resume or start fresh. \n\nYou’ll leave with real progress made-maybe even a finished draft! Upcoming Resume 1.0 Workshops Ready to find your next gig? Discover effective job search strategies, leverage Handshake, and learn the importance of networking to land your dream job. Upcoming Job Search Basics Workshops Want to ace your next job interview? Learn the STAR method for answering tough questions, craft a memorable introduction, and discover tips that will help you stand out from the competition. Upcoming Interviewing Workshops Ready to make a splash at a job fair? Explore career resources, research potential employers, and create a personalized strategy maximize your experience. Upcoming Job Fair Prep Workshops Next Step In-Person, Drop-In Career Advice Common career questions can quickly be addressed through drop-in advising - no appointment necessary! Students with questions regarding resumes, cover letters, activating their Handshake account, or navigating any job search resources can work with well-trained student career ambassadors to by vising any of the four drop-in locations. Drop-in advice sessions typically take between 10 and 20 minutes. Drop-in Career Advising is not offered during the summer and will begin in September 2026. Still Need Support Career Coaching Students can also sign up to work with a professional Career Development Specialist by making an appointment. Career Coaching is designed to assist those students who are looking for a deeper level of assistance including: Helping decide between career fields or majors. Assistance with a job search - often after applying to several jobs unsuccessfully. Identifying and developing personal talents into strengths and how to leverage them in a job search. Career Coaching may be completed in one session or may involve multiple sessions - either way the Career Development Specialist is available to you until you have achieved your goal. Undergraduate Students Book a Career Coaching Appointment through the Student Success Hub Book a Career Coaching Appointment Graduate Students and Alumni Book a Career Coaching Appointment through Handshake. Book a Career Coaching Appointment Alumni who no longer have access to your WMU login please e-mail wmu-handshake@wmich.edu with your name, a WMU identifier (WIN, BNID, or @wmich.edu e-mail address) and graduation year to have your handshake account switched to your personal e-mail address. Footer menu Audiences Alumni and Donors Businesses Veterans Locations Grand Rapids Kalamazoo Online Education Stryker School of Medicine Services Accessibility Campus Safety Information and Resources Human Resources Maps Parking Western Michigan University Kalamazoo MI 49008-5200 USA (269) 387-1000 Contact WMU WMU Notice of Non-Discrimination Land Acknowledgment Statement © 2026 All rights reserved. Social"
    },
    "https://wmich.edu/career/students/headshots": {
      "title": "Headshots",
      "description": "Headshots | Career and Student Employment Services | Western Michigan University Skip to main content Top links Apply A–Z Find People goWMU Visit Keywords Main navigation Academics Admissions Financial Aid Student Life Athletics Research Give Main Menu Close Menu Keywords Top links Apply A–Z Find People goWMU Visit Home Explore Career Options Student Resources Resumes Cover Letters Interviews Job Fair Preparation Services for Students Job Postings Career Academy Resume Reviews Virtual Practice Interviews Career Coaching Headshots Employers Post an Opportunity Internships Engage on Campus International Students Bronco Engagement Faculty and Staff Campus Employment For Students For Supervisors Pay Rates Work Study Student Appreciation Events Event Preparation Request a Presentation Career Outcomes About Us Directory Our Student Staff Contact Us Main navigation Academics Admissions Financial Aid Student Life Athletics Research Give Career and Student Employment Services Headshots Career and Student Employment Services Skip to content Group menu sidebar Home Explore Career Options Student Resources Resumes Cover Letters Interviews Job Fair Preparation Services for Students Job Postings Career Academy Resume Reviews Virtual Practice Interviews Career Coaching Headshots Employers Post an Opportunity Internships Engage on Campus International Students Bronco Engagement Faculty and Staff Campus Employment For Students For Supervisors Pay Rates Work Study Student Appreciation Events Event Preparation Request a Presentation Career Outcomes About Us Directory Our Student Staff Contact Us Career and Student Employment Services Western Michigan University Kalamazoo MI 49008-5225 USA (269) 387-2745 Headshots Ready to have your headshot taken? Sign up today for a free professional headshot session, brought to you by WMU staff! An updated headshot isn’t just a photo—it’s your first impression, your introduction, and your story all rolled into one. Whether you’re updating your LinkedIn profile picture or taking the opportunity to create a post to share your story in a professional manner. Join us at the Student Center for a relaxed and fun experience that’s all about showcasing YOU at your best. No need to worry about awkward poses or stiff smiles—we will guide you every step of the way. Sign up now and take the first step toward building connections and opening doors to exciting opportunities! All headshots are taken in Career Lab (2206) in the WMU Student Center, located on the middle floor of the WMU Student Center, behind the main staircase. Sign up for 10-minute Headshot Appointment Drop-In Hours Headshots are available by drop-ins as well, though we encourage students to make an appointment. Drop-in headshots are not guaranteed and only available if the photographer is free. Stop by The Source (2206) in the WMU Student Center to get your headshot taken. Fall 2026 Drop-In Hours: Fridays 11am-5pm Footer menu Audiences Alumni and Donors Businesses Veterans Locations Grand Rapids Kalamazoo Online Education Stryker School of Medicine Services Accessibility Campus Safety Information and Resources Human Resources Maps Parking Western Michigan University Kalamazoo MI 49008-5200 USA (269) 387-1000 Contact WMU WMU Notice of Non-Discrimination Land Acknowledgment Statement © 2026 All rights reserved. Social"
