    "https://wmich.edu/career/events/eventprep": {
      "title": "Career Event Preparation",
      "description": "Career Event Preparation | Career and Student Employment Services | Western Michigan University Skip to main content Top links Apply A–Z Find People goWMU Visit Keywords Main navigation Academics Admissions Financial Aid Student Life Athletics Research Give Main Menu Close Menu Keywords Top links Apply A–Z Find People goWMU Visit Home Explore Career Options Student Resources Resumes Cover Letters Interviews Job Fair Preparation Services for Students Job Postings Career Academy Resume Reviews Virtual Practice Interviews Career Coaching Headshots Employers Post an Opportunity Internships Engage on Campus International Students Bronco Engagement Faculty and Staff Campus Employment For Students For Supervisors Pay Rates Work Study Student Appreciation Events Event Preparation Request a Presentation Career Outcomes About Us Directory Our Student Staff Contact Us Main navigation Academics Admissions Financial Aid Student Life Athletics Research Give Career and Student Employment Services Events Career Event Preparation Career and Student Employment Services Skip to content Group menu sidebar Home Explore Career Options Student Resources Resumes Cover Letters Interviews Job Fair Preparation Services for Students Job Postings Career Academy Resume Reviews Virtual Practice Interviews Career Coaching Headshots Employers Post an Opportunity Internships Engage on Campus International Students Bronco Engagement Faculty and Staff Campus Employment For Students For Supervisors Pay Rates Work Study Student Appreciation Events Event Preparation Request a Presentation Career Outcomes About Us Directory Our Student Staff Contact Us Career and Student Employment Services Western Michigan University Kalamazoo MI 49008-5225 USA (269) 387-2745 Career Event Preparation Event preparation resources Virtual job fairs and interviews resource guide Learn what to do before, during and after a job fair . Do your research! One of the most impressive things to a recruiter is knowledge of the company, culture, their products, and their available positions. Look at the company website, do some research online, find them in Handshake . Resumes and cover letters : review the Career Development Guide , and be sure to have your documents looked at by an advisor . Interview preparation : explore the resources available at Big Interview - decide if the fast track or mastery course is right for you, and choose from numerous categories and thousands of questions. Dress for success . View our upcoming career preparation events in Handshake . If you are a recruiter interested in participating in preparation activities, please call (269) 387-2745 and ask for Buffy or email her at buffy.m.nespodzany@wmich.edu. Footer menu Audiences Alumni and Donors Businesses Veterans Locations Grand Rapids Kalamazoo Online Education Stryker School of Medicine Services Accessibility Campus Safety Information and Resources Human Resources Maps Parking Western Michigan University Kalamazoo MI 49008-5200 USA (269) 387-1000 Contact WMU WMU Notice of Non-Discrimination Land Acknowledgment Statement © 2026 All rights reserved. Social"
