    "https://wmich.edu/career/about": {
      "title": "About Career and Student Employment Services",
      "description": "About Career and Student Employment Services | Career and Student Employment Services | Western Michigan University Skip to main content Top links Apply A–Z Find People goWMU Visit Keywords Main navigation Academics Admissions Financial Aid Student Life Athletics Research Give Main Menu Close Menu Keywords Top links Apply A–Z Find People goWMU Visit Home Explore Career Options Student Resources Resumes Cover Letters Interviews Job Fair Preparation Services for Students Job Postings Career Academy Resume Reviews Virtual Practice Interviews Career Coaching Headshots Employers Post an Opportunity Internships Engage on Campus International Students Bronco Engagement Faculty and Staff Campus Employment For Students For Supervisors Pay Rates Work Study Student Appreciation Events Event Preparation Request a Presentation Career Outcomes About Us Directory Our Student Staff Contact Us Main navigation Academics Admissions Financial Aid Student Life Athletics Research Give Career and Student Employment Services About Career and Student Employment Services Career and Student Employment Services Skip to content Group menu sidebar Home Explore Career Options Student Resources Resumes Cover Letters Interviews Job Fair Preparation Services for Students Job Postings Career Academy Resume Reviews Virtual Practice Interviews Career Coaching Headshots Employers Post an Opportunity Internships Engage on Campus International Students Bronco Engagement Faculty and Staff Campus Employment For Students For Supervisors Pay Rates Work Study Student Appreciation Events Event Preparation Request a Presentation Career Outcomes About Us Directory Our Student Staff Contact Us Career and Student Employment Services Western Michigan University Kalamazoo MI 49008-5225 USA (269) 387-2745 About Career and Student Employment Services Career and Student Employment Services at Western Michigan University is here to support students to secure jobs. We assist students during any part of their job search process including career exploration, learning job search basics, getting an on-campus job or part-time job in the community, securing an internship, and finding full-time employment after graduation. All WMU graduates actively engaged in a position they are satisfied with, related to their chosen career field, within three mons of their graduation. — Career and Student Employment Services Vision Career and Student Employment Services Themes How we accomplish our mission and work towards our vision. Experience-Driven Learning Equip students with diverse, resume-worth experiences that build essential skills and career readiness. Career Coaching Guide students in articulating their experiences and strengths, and support them through the job search. Community Connections Cultivate robust partnerships with employers, community eorganizations, and alumni to create a network of opportunities for students. Career and Student Employment Services Values Equity We provide each student, staff member, and partner with what they need to be successful, honoring their unique experiences, needs, and backgrounds. Relationships We cultivate genuine, respectful, and collaborative relationships with students, colleagues, and partners, fostering a community of trust and shared purpose. Strengths We celebrate and leverage the unique talents, experiences, and perspectives that each person brings. Future Focused We inspire students to achieve their long-term aspirations while embracing forward-thinking approaches, constantly evolving our services to stay at the forefront of career services . Integrity We act with honesty, transparency, and accountability to uphold our commitments. Excellence We relentlessly pursue the highest standards in all that we do, fostering a culture of continuous improvement. Footer menu Audiences Alumni and Donors Businesses Veterans Locations Grand Rapids Kalamazoo Online Education Stryker School of Medicine Services Accessibility Campus Safety Information and Resources Human Resources Maps Parking Western Michigan University Kalamazoo MI 49008-5200 USA (269) 387-1000 Contact WMU WMU Notice of Non-Discrimination Land Acknowledgment Statement © 2026 All rights reserved. Social"
    },
